      "writtenOn": "2015-02-24T06:51:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Did not benchmark, stole the code from cl:246181\n\nWe probably wait too much. Anyway, instead of clock_wait_bus_cycles(), I think the proper way should be to use the third work around proposed by ST:\n\"\"\"3.     Enable the peripheral clock well ahead of time when the peripheral read/write register access is required. (Note, NOPs aren’t a reliable way to add delays)\"\"\"\n\nWe know at compile time which module we are going to need.\nThis require some refactoring though.",
      "parentUuid": "88ae1292_387129f8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 15
      },
